{
 "_comment": "LTX-2.3 IC-LoRA UNION CONTROL: a control video (depth here, via MoGe-2) steers the shot's structure and camera while the start frame sets the look. Flattened from ComfyUI's own template video_ltx2_3_ic_lora by scripts/ui2api.py and rewired to the checkpoint this box has. The same LoRA reads canny (core Canny node) and pose (SDPose, workflow 27) maps. Measured 2026-09-17 by studio/_tools/ic_lora_test.py (LTX_PLAYBOOK §97.2): a depth guide made LTX-2.3 pull back 27% against a 26% rig on 3 of 3 seeds (zoom-curve RMSE 0.008), where the same words alone pushed in 17-47%.",
 "_notes": [
  "Inputs: node 199 LoadVideo = the control clip (121 frames, the output's aspect); node 200 LoadImage = the start frame, which should BE the look of the control clip's first frame - the guide and the picture have to agree at frame 0.",
  "The template loads ltx-2.3-22b-distilled-fp8, which this box never downloaded (STATE.md). It runs on dev-fp8 + the distilled LoRA at 0.5, as ComfyUI's own ID-LoRA template does.",
  "GetICLoRAParameters reads the LoRA's reference_downscale_factor (ref0.5) and hands it to LTXVAddGuide; LTXVCropGuides strips the guide frames before decoding. Do not remove either.",
  "Feed the raw MoGe 'depth' render, never 'depth_colored' - a colormap is read as content.",
  "Seed: sg1_704 (KSampler, 8 steps, euler_ancestral, linear_quadratic, cfg 1).",
  "Changes from the template: checkpoint -> dev-fp8 + distilled LoRA; the prompt enhancer and its abliterated Gemma LoRA removed; two links ui2api mis-resolved repaired (GetVideoComponents.video, MoGeInference.batch_size); the 5 s video slice removed and the length pinned at 121; unused MoGe outputs removed."
 ],
